{"name":"Roulette","hex":"#97635f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"roulette","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A game of chance in which a small ball is made to move round rapidly on a circle divided off into numbered (usually red and black) spaces. When the ball stops, it indicates the result of a variety of wagers permitted by the game.","An instance of risk-taking, especially when the downside exceeds the upside (contrary to the game of roulette where only the wager is lost)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To separate or decorate by incisions made with a small toothed wheel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/roulette"}],"entries":[{"title":"Roulette","blocks":[{"text":"Roulette is a casino game which was likely developed from the Italian game Biribi. In the game, a player may choose to place a bet on a single number, various groupings of numbers, the color red or black, whether the number is odd or even, or if the number is high or low."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/13-02-27-spielbank-wiesbaden-by-RalfR-094.jpg/330px-13-02-27-spielbank-wiesbaden-by-RalfR-094.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roulette"},{"title":"Roulette (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Roulette is the fourth studio album by English boy band Blue, released from 25 January 2013 through Blueworld and Island Records. Their first studio album in ten years, Blue began working on the project in 2010 with a number of American musicians such as Bruno Mars and Ne-Yo, though it was eventually significantly reworked, invlolving production from a range of different producers such as Cufather & Joe, Steve DuBerry, RedOne, and Lucas Secon, among others. Band members Lee Ryan, Duncan James, Antony Costa, and Simon Webbe co-wrote on several tracks on the album."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/05/Blueroulette.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roulette_(album)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Gwendolen_Harleth.jpg/500px-Gwendolen_Harleth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Gwendolen_Harleth.jpg/1280px-Gwendolen_Harleth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Gwendolen_Harleth.jpg/500px-Gwendolen_Harleth.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Gwendolen at the roulette table\" – 1910 illustration to George Eliot's Daniel Deronda","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGwendolen_Harleth.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/76/EO_Wheel.jpg/500px-EO_Wheel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/76/EO_Wheel.jpg/500px-EO_Wheel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"18th-century E.O. wheel with gamblers","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEO_Wheel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Flemish_characters_by_James_Gillray_%282%29.jpg/500px-Flemish_characters_by_James_Gillray_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Flemish_characters_by_James_Gillray_%282%29.jpg/1280px-Flemish_characters_by_James_Gillray_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Flemish_characters_by_James_Gillray_%282%29.jpg/500px-Flemish_characters_by_James_Gillray_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th